WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.139
"The Lion fell asleep too," said the Tin Man.

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:07.311
The Scarecrow nodded.

3
00:00:07.312 --> 00:00:12.448
"I'm sorry to leave him here, but we'd better take Dorothy to safety."

4
00:00:12.449 --> 00:00:15.532
"We can't be far from the road," said the Tin Man.

5
00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:21.386
As soon as he spoke, the road seemed to appear.

6
00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:25.991
"Will Dorothy sleep forever?" asked the Tin Man impatiently.

7
00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:29.108
"I don't know," said the Scarecrow.

8
00:00:29.109 --> 00:00:33.606
"I wish I had a brain so I could think of a way to help the Lion too."

9
00:00:33.607 --> 00:00:37.651
Suddenly a large cat came bounding out of the woods.

10
00:00:37.652 --> 00:00:43.814
It was chasing a tiny gray field mouse.

11
00:00:43.815 --> 00:00:49.072
As the mouse ran by, the Tin Man raised his ax and shouted, "Stop!"

12
00:00:49.073 --> 00:00:52.002
The cat saw the Tin Man and froze.

13
00:00:52.003 --> 00:00:57.830
Just as the Tin Man swung his ax, the cat jumped and ran back into the woods.

14
00:00:57.831 --> 00:01:02.715
"Thank you for saving my life," said the mouse.

15
00:01:02.716 --> 00:01:05.409
"Don't mention it," said the Tin Man.

16
00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:10.743
"I have no heart so I am careful to help everyone, even a mouse."

17
00:01:10.744 --> 00:01:14.499
"Even a mouse?" she said indignantly.

18
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.892
"Why, I am the Queen of all the field mice!"

19
00:01:18.893 --> 00:01:26.037
"Oh!" said the Tin Man as he noticed her crown and several other mice behind her.

20
00:01:26.038 --> 00:01:33.486
"You have saved my life," said the Queen. "I owe you a favor."

21
00:01:33.487 --> 00:01:37.134
Just then Toto woke up and barked, causing the mice to run.

22
00:01:37.135 --> 00:01:39.750
The Tin Man took Toto in his arms.

23
00:01:39.751 --> 00:01:44.632
"Come back! Come back! Toto will not hurt you!" shouted the Tin Man.

24
00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:49.358
"I promise, Toto won't hurt you."

25
00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:53.965
"Are you sure he will not bite us?" asked the Queen.

26
00:01:53.966 --> 00:01:57.450
"I won't let him," said the Tin Man firmly.

27
00:01:57.451 --> 00:02:06.923
The mice returned, and the biggest mouse looked at the Tin Man and asked, "How can we repay you for saving the Queen?"

28
00:02:06.924 --> 00:02:10.910
"We need help rescuing a friend," said the Scarecrow.

29
00:02:10.911 --> 00:02:16.121
"We are small," said the Queen. "How can we help?"

30
00:02:16.122 --> 00:02:19.575
"Are there many of you?" asked the Scarecrow.

31
00:02:19.576 --> 00:02:24.343
"Yes, there are thousands of us," answered the Queen.

32
00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:32.149
"Bring them all, and a lot of string," said the Scarecrow.

33
00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:39.581
Now Dorothy woke up and walked over to her friends.

34
00:02:39.582 --> 00:02:41.979
"Tin Man," said the Scarecrow.

35
00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.427
"I need you to build us a cart so we can carry the Lion on it."

36
00:02:46.428 --> 00:02:51.028
The Tin Man began to chop down trees and make the cart.

37
00:02:51.029 --> 00:02:55.202
Soon the mice returned, and there were many thousands of them.

38
00:02:55.203 --> 00:03:00.576
The Scarecrow and the Tin Man pushed the Lion onto the cart.

39
00:03:00.577 --> 00:03:04.288
"Okay! He's on!" shouted the Tin Man.

40
00:03:04.289 --> 00:03:07.521
"Pull!" shouted the Queen to her subjects.

41
00:03:07.522 --> 00:03:13.240
Slowly at first, and then more swiftly, the cart began to move.

42
00:03:13.241 --> 00:03:23.391
"If you ever need us again, just come to the field and call," said the Queen. "We will hear you."

43
00:03:23.392 --> 00:03:27.800
Soon the Lion began to stir.

44
00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:34.715
"I ran as fast as I could, but the flowers were too strong," he murmured.

45
00:03:34.716 --> 00:03:36.989
"How did you move me?"

46
00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:45.297
The Scarecrow and the Tin Man explained that the mice had saved him. The Lion laughed.

47
00:03:45.298 --> 00:03:56.439
"I have always thought myself very big and terrible, yet flowers almost killed me, and some mice saved my life."

48
00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.116
"I wonder if we are close to Oz," said Dorothy.

49
00:04:00.117 --> 00:04:06.188
"I don't know," said the Scarecrow. "But there is one way to find out."

50
00:04:06.189 --> 00:04:15.135
The group happily returned to the road, and they were relieved because they thought they had left their adventures behind them.

51
00:04:15.136 --> 00:04:19.096
"We must be in the land of Oz," said Dorothy.

52
00:04:19.097 --> 00:04:21.604
"Yes," said the Scarecrow.

53
00:04:21.605 --> 00:04:27.308
"The favorite color here seems to be green, as it probably is in the Emerald City."

54
00:04:27.309 --> 00:04:32.175
"It is getting dark," said Dorothy. "We will need to stop for the night."

55
00:04:32.176 --> 00:04:37.952
At the next farmhouse, Dorothy bravely knocked.

56
00:04:37.953 --> 00:04:40.970
"Yes?" said the woman at the door.

57
00:04:40.971 --> 00:04:43.970
"Can we spend the night?" asked Dorothy.

58
00:04:43.971 --> 00:04:48.671
"That depends. Is your lion tame?" asked the woman.

59
00:04:48.672 --> 00:04:55.118
"Oh yes," said Dorothy. "He is a coward and wouldn't hurt a fly."

60
00:04:55.119 --> 00:05:03.590
"Okay," said the woman. "You may stay here tonight. Where are you headed?"

61
00:05:03.591 --> 00:05:07.655
"We are going to see the Wizard of Oz," answered Dorothy.

62
00:05:07.656 --> 00:05:11.141
"I don't think you will see the Wizard," said the woman.

63
00:05:11.142 --> 00:05:21.060
"I have been to the Emerald City many times, and I have never seen him."

